**As a** command-line user
**I want** to run `{{kebab .Name}}` and get a greeting
**So that** the scaffold's spec → test → verify loop is proven end to end

**Independent test:** `mise run -C {{.Dir}} test` proves the scenarios below
against the headless library (the executable is a thin shell over it).

# Acceptance Criteria

## Scenario 1: greeting a name returns a friendly line

<!-- id: scenario.greet.run.basic -->

- Given a name
- When the tool greets it
- Then the line reads "Hello, <name>!"

## Scenario 2: the shout flag upper-cases the greeting

<!-- id: scenario.greet.run.shout -->

- Given a name and the --shout flag
- When the tool greets it
- Then the greeting is upper-cased
